    "eval and dynamically constructed code",
    "raw HTML injection points (innerHTML, dangerouslySetInnerHTML, v-html)",
    "errors that are caught and silently discarded",
    "error handling removed without replacement",
    "images without alternative text",
    "focus indicators removed without a visible replacement",
    "click handlers on non-interactive elements without keyboard support",
    "workflow token permissions broadened to write-all",
    "behavior changes without accompanying tests",
    "major-version dependency upgrades",
    "new environment variables missing from env examples",
    "tests that are newly skipped or disabled",
    "debugger statements and breakpoints left in application code",
    "mismatch between the stated intent and what the change does",
  ],
  "findings": [],
}
`;

exports[`English output (baseline) > refactor-retry-helper > writes the same rule findings, explanation, and reports > summary.md 1`] = `
"## Extract backoff calculation from the retry loop

This change extracts backoff calculation from the retry loop in http. It touches 3 files across \`http\` and \`test\` (+27 −3). No user-facing surface (UI, API, or CLI) is touched.

**Changes**

- **http**: Adds \`backoffDelay\` and changes \`withRetry\`.
- **test**: Edits \`backoff.test.js\`.

**Review focus**

- \`src/http/backoff.js\`: Adds \`backoffDelay\`.
- \`src/http/retry.js\`: Changes \`withRetry\`.

**Testing**

- 2 test cases added across 1 test file
"
`;

